## 3.2 SYSTEMATIC FAILURE

### Domestic Epistemic Measurement

**Conceptual definition:**

Systematic Failure describes the breakdown, omission, or ineffective implementation of institutional safeguards intended to protect evidentiary reliability, procedural fairness, scientific independence, and public accountability.

The domestic dimension requires particular care because family matters, emergency interventions, civil proceedings, healthcare decisions, and scientific oversight operate under different authorities and evidentiary standards.

